.TH AETHER 1 "October 2026" "Aether 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
aether \- high-assurance Linux threat hunter and forensic triage engine
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B aether
[\fB\-\-config\fR \fIPATH\fR]
[\fB\-\-verbose\fR]
[\fB\-\-debug\fR]
[\fB\-\-quiet\fR]
[\fB\-\-plain\fR]
[\fB\-\-no\-anim\fR]
\fICOMMAND\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBAether\fR is an executive-grade, forensic-safe, read-only Linux threat hunting and anomaly detection platform. It performs deep static heuristic analysis, embedded YARA-X signature evaluation, runtime process/network correlation, persistence inspection, and package integrity verification across Linux endpoints and cloud infrastructure.
.PP
Aether strictly enforces static inspection invariants: it \fBNEVER\fR executes scanned target binaries or scripts, never mutates inspected files, and requires zero external network connectivity.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B scan
Perform customizable threat hunting scan on specified paths or root filesystem. See \fBaether-scan\fR(1).
.TP
.B quick
Execute rapid triage scan of high-risk operational directories (/tmp, /var/tmp, /dev/shm, user home directories, persistence hooks).
.TP
.B full
Execute deep, exhaustive filesystem-wide threat hunt across all mounted local partitions.
.TP
.B setup
Perform automated self-test, verify permissions, inspect kernel BPF/ptrace capabilities, and test rule loading.
.TP
.B ack
Acknowledge and suppress benign operational anomalies using cryptographic hash pinning. See \fBaether-ack\fR(1).
.TP
.B rules
Inspect, validate, and manage embedded and custom YARA rule sets. See \fBaether-rules\fR(1).
.TP
.B version
Print version metadata, git commit, build date, Go runtime, OS/architecture, and active threat engine status.
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-c ", " \-\-config " PATH"
Path to custom YAML configuration file (default: \fI/etc/aether/config.yaml\fR or \fI~/.config/aether/config.yaml\fR).
.TP
.B \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Enable detailed verbose event logging.
.TP
.B \-d ", " \-\-debug
Enable diagnostic debug logging to standard error.
.TP
.B \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Suppress interactive dashboard; emit only summary results.
.TP
.B \-\-plain
Force plain non-color, non-interactive ANSI output (suitable for headless servers and cron jobs).
.TP
.B \-\-no\-anim
Disable terminal spinner and layout animations.
.SH SECURITY & FORENSIC INVARIANTS
.TP
.B Read-Only Inspection
Files are opened with \fBO_NOFOLLOW | O_CLOEXEC | O_NONBLOCK | O_NOATIME\fR to prevent symlink traversal attacks, FIFO pipe blocking, and access-time metadata contamination.
.TP
.B Zero Scanned Execution
Threat evaluation uses strictly static AST parsing, ELF header inspection, regex heuristics, and compiled YARA-X pattern matching. No target payload is ever dynamically invoked.
.TP
.B Offline Integrity
Aether operates 100% locally and contains zero telemetry, analytics, or remote network phone-home capabilities.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/aether/config.yaml
System-wide configuration file.
.TP
.I /etc/aether/rules/
System-wide custom YARA rule directory.
.TP
.I /var/log/aether/
Standard destination for audit reports and scan logs.
.TP
.I /etc/aether/acknowledged.yaml
System-wide triage acknowledgment registry.
.SH DISCLAIMER & CLAIM DISCIPLINE
Aether is an automated security audit and threat hunting tool. While engineered for rigorous detection accuracy and zero false positives on known threat patterns, no automated software can guarantee detection of all novel, customized, or zero-day attacks. Threat hunting output must be evaluated in context with comprehensive defense-in-depth security practices.
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBaether-scan\fR(1), \fBaether-ack\fR(1), \fBaether-rules\fR(1)
